(1. Linear Algebra: Matrix Decompositions & Eigenvalues) Tj
/F2 10 Tf
0 -16 Td
(A symmetric matrix A in R^\(n x n\) can be orthogonally diagonalized as A = Q * Lambda * Q^T.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Here, Q is an orthogonal matrix whose columns are orthonormal eigenvectors of A,) Tj
0 -16 Td
(and Lambda is a diagonal matrix containing the real eigenvalues of A.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Key property: Trace\(A\) equals the sum of eigenvalues, and Det\(A\) equals their product.) Tj
